## Codebase Patterns
- The component uses `WebComponent.create('image-editor')` for registration.
- Authored light-DOM content is captured in `connectedCallback()` before the
  base class invokes `render()`.
- Reflected attributes use exact HTML names in the base class; kebab-case
  attributes can expose a typed camel-case accessor backed by that attribute.
- Corner affordances keep their cursor direction in the rendered handle style
  as well as the stylesheet, so the direction remains observable and stable
  during later pointer interaction work.
- Pure resize calculations live in `src/resize-math.ts`; DOM and pointer
  orchestration stays in `src/index.ts`.
- DOM observers are created after base-class rendering and disconnected in the
  custom element lifecycle.
- Numeric kebab-case attributes use `reflectedStringAttributes` with typed
  camel-case accessors; getters validate the attribute source before passing
  values into pure interaction math.

