## 2026-08-25 03:30 - US-005
- Implemented canvas blob production when pointer resizing ends.
- The component sizes an offscreen canvas to the final visual dimensions,
  prefers `createImageBitmap`, falls back to the captured image, closes any
  bitmap, and emits `image-editor:resize-end` with `{ blob, width, height }`.
- Added browser coverage for both bitmap and fallback draw paths, updated
  runtime architecture documentation, and marked US-005 complete.
- Files changed: `src/index.ts`, `test/index.ts`,
  `docs/architecture/runtime-component.md`,
  `docs/architecture/runtime-state.md`, `specs/prd.json`, `progress.log`.
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - Canvas output is transient and should not become component state; only
    the emitted blob and dimensions cross the public event boundary.
  - Browser tests can replace canvas methods and restore them after asserting
    draw source, canvas dimensions, and blob output.
